/T (These results are largely consistent with those observed in FY2022-23, with several notable exceptions in related behavioral areas. In particular, there was a nearly two-fold increase in Arizonans reporting problems with video gaming \(3.0% vs. 1.5%\) and an 84% increase in problems with mobile phone gaming \(3.4% vs. 1.8%\). The observed increases may reflect broader trends in digital engagement and the growing convergence between gaming and gambling-like activities, as discussed below.)
