>>
endobj
5343 0 obj
<<
/Title (Arizonans were more likely to report attempting to quit or cut down a behavior than to report the behavior as problematic \(9% versus 5%\). The rate of reporting behavior as problematic was similar to the rate of others expressing concern \(4.8% versus 4.6%\).)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5248 0 R
/Prev 5315 0 R
/Next 5359 0 R
>>
endobj
5344 0 obj
<<
/Title (These results are largely consistent with those observed in FY2022-23, with several notable exceptions in related behavioral areas. In particular, there was a nearly two-fold increase in Arizonans reporting problems with video gaming \(3.0% vs. 1.5%\) and an 84% increase in problems with mobile phone gaming \(3.4% vs. 1.8%\). The observed increases may reflect broader trends in digital engagement and the growing convergence between gaming and gambling-like activities, as discussed below.)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5248 0 R
/Prev 5359 0 R
/Next 5316 0 R
>>
endobj
5345 0 obj
<<
/Title (SUMMARY OF SURVEY FINDINGS 2026)
